---
pagination:
  data: cities
  size: 1
  alias: c
  # Without this Eleventy adds ONLY the first paginated page to collections,
  # so the sitemap and llms.txt would list Auckland and omit the other five.
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "/tradie-websites-{{ c.slug }}/"
# `| safe` on every passthrough is load-bearing, not decoration. These strings
# are rendered here and then rendered AGAIN by whatever outputs them (the layout,
# the meta tags, the schema). Without `safe` an apostrophe is escaped to `&#39;`
# on this pass and the `&` is escaped to `&amp;` on the next, so the page shows
# a literal "website&#39;s". Escaping belongs at the point of output, once.
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ c.title | safe }}"
  description: "{{ c.description | safe }}"
  eyebrow: "{{ c.city | upper | safe }}"
  heading: "{{ c.heading | safe }}"
  intro: "{{ c.intro | safe }}"
  breadcrumbName: "Tradie websites {{ c.city | safe }}"
---
{% extends "layouts/page.njk" %}

{% block schema %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Service",
        "@id": "{{ site.url }}/tradie-websites-{{ c.slug }}/#service",
        "name": "Tradie website design in {{ c.city }}",
        "serviceType": "Website design for trade businesses in {{ c.city }}",
        "provider": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#business" },
        "description": {{ c.description | dump | safe }},
        "areaServed": {
          "@type": "City",
          "name": "{{ c.city }}",
          "containedInPlace": { "@type": "AdministrativeArea", "name": "{{ c.region }}, New Zealand" }
        },
        "audience": {
          "@type": "BusinessAudience",
          "name": "Trade businesses in {{ c.city }}"
        },
        "offers": {
          "@type": "Offer",
          "price": "{{ site.price }}",
          "priceCurrency": "{{ site.currency }}",
          "availability": "https://schema.org/InStock",
          "url": "{{ site.url }}/tradie-websites-{{ c.slug }}/",
          "seller": { "@id": "{{ site.url }}/#organization" }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "@id": "{{ site.url }}/tradie-websites-{{ c.slug }}/#faq",
        "mainEntity": [{% for item in c.faqs %}
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": {{ item.q | dump | safe }},
            "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.a | dump | safe }} }
          }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>
{% endblock %}

{% block prose %}
<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>{{ site.priceDisplay }} flat, live in {{ site.buildDays }}.</strong> Copywriting, local SEO, .nz domain and Google Business Profile setup included — with the Jobs In {{ site.guaranteeDays }} Guarantee.</p>
</div>

<h2>What the {{ c.city }} market is actually like</h2>
<p>{{ c.localMarket }}</p>

<h2>How {{ c.city }} customers search</h2>
<p>{{ c.searchBehaviour }}</p>

<h2>What we build into a {{ c.city }} tradie's site</h2>
{%- for f in c.localFactors %}
<h3>{{ f.title }}</h3>
<p>{{ f.body }}</p>
{%- endfor %}

<h2>Areas we'll target for you</h2>
<p>Your build includes suburb and service-area targeting. For a {{ c.city }} business that usually means some combination of:</p>
<ul class="suburb-list">
  {%- for s in c.suburbs %}
  <li>{{ s }}</li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
<p>We pick the ones you actually service on the kickoff call. Fewer real areas beats a long list of thin pages — Google spots padded location pages, and so do customers.</p>

<h2>Questions from {{ c.city }} tradies</h2>
{%- for item in c.faqs %}
<h3>{{ item.q }}</h3>
<p>{{ item.a }}</p>
{%- endfor %}

<hr />

<h2>Built for your trade as well as your city</h2>
<p>The local targeting above sits on top of a site written for what you actually do:</p>
<ul class="trade-links">
  {%- for t in trades %}
  <li><a href="/websites-for-{{ t.slug }}/">Websites for {{ t.plural }}</a></li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>What it costs</h2>
<p><strong>{{ site.priceDisplay }}</strong>, one time — build, copywriting, local SEO foundation, .nz domain, {{ site.hostingIncluded }} and Google Business Profile setup. First ten founding clients pay {{ site.foundingPriceDisplay }}. Full breakdown on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>.</p>

<h2>Ready to get found in {{ c.city }}?</h2>
<p>Book a kickoff call. Thirty minutes, and we'll tell you honestly whether we can move the needle for your trade in your part of {{ c.city }} — including if we can't.</p>
<p><a href="/#contact" class="btn large">BOOK MY KICKOFF CALL →</a></p>

<hr />

<h2>We also build for tradies in</h2>
<ul class="trade-links">
  {%- for other in cities %}{% if other.slug != c.slug %}
  <li><a href="/tradie-websites-{{ other.slug }}/">{{ other.city }}</a></li>
  {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>
<p>Somewhere else in New Zealand? We build nationwide — <a href="/#contact">tell us where you are</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
